  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "L5 analogs M01 and M16 share the query's acrylamide-piperidine-4-aminopyrazolo[3,4-d]pyrimidine core and show no appreciable gut-wall efflux (Caco-2 efflux ratios 1.03 and 0.66) with high A-to-B permeability (Papp 11.81 in source units), indicating gut-wall efflux is unlikely to limit the query's absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C174", "C177", "C208"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The closest L3 analog (M02) with the same 4-phenoxyphenyl-pyrazolopyrimidine-piperidine amide core is rapidly absorbed in humans (median Tmax 0.5-1 h), supporting oral absorption of this scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C72", "C105", "C91", "C109"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 acalabrutinib records show high permeability (MDCK-MDR1 Papp 15.2 x 10^-6 cm/s; effective Peff 5.4 x 10^-4 cm/s) and rapid dissolution, supporting the absorption component; solubility is moderate and formulation-dependent, and the query's higher logD is a caveat rather than affirmative low-F evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C128", "C144", "C158", "C125", "C156", "C123", "C133", "C152"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Acalabrutinib is reported as a P-gp/BCRP substrate, but this is a different core and substrate status alone is not a low-F outcome; the same-scaffold M01/M16 records show no efflux, so this does not overturn the high prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C194", "C201", "C174", "C177", "C208"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C174", "C177", "C208"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability or IV/oral AUC comparison is available.",
    "No direct F value is reported for the query or its closest analogs (M02, M01, M16).",
    "No query-specific fasted-state solubility or dissolution measurement is available; high logD/logP is only a proxy.",
    "No query-specific first-pass hepatic metabolism or clearance data are available; the acrylamide warhead and high lipophilicity are unquantified risks.",
    "No formulation or clinical dose is specified for the query, so the impact of solubility on F cannot be quantified."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 same-scaffold analogs show no gut-wall efflux and high permeability, strengthening the absorption evidence from L3/L4. No transferable direct low-F outcome exists for the query or its closest analogs; solubility and first-pass metabolism remain unmeasured caveats. F >= 20% remains better supported; prediction high with moderate confidence."
}

